WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.538
This is the Lesson 2.1 deck. Now we add a truck: baseplate, hanger and axle, bushing, and kingpin.

00:00:11.088 --> 00:00:18.182
Right-click Part 1 → Rename → Deck.

00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:23.643
Bottom view. Start a sketch on the bottom face of the deck.

00:00:24.193 --> 00:00:30.056
Show Sketch 2 (the bolt holes) with its eye icon.

00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:39.395
Offset tool: pick the 4 lines of the bolt-hole rectangle, arrow outward, 0.25 in.

00:00:39.945 --> 00:00:45.401
The bigger rectangle is the baseplate outline.

00:00:45.951 --> 00:00:51.095
Extrude: New, 0.25 in, away from the deck.

00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:55.255
A new grey plate under the deck.

00:00:55.805 --> 00:01:00.879
Sketch on the Front plane. Use tool: bring in the plate's bottom edge.

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:05.423
Corner rectangle under the plate, from the end of that edge.

00:01:05.973 --> 00:01:10.582
A second, smaller rectangle below it, lined up on the right.

00:01:11.132 --> 00:01:18.655
Dimensions: 0.5 and 0.375 tall, 1.5 wide for the lower block.

00:01:19.205 --> 00:01:27.622
Extrude: Add to the plate, 0.75 in, Symmetric.

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:31.853
Rename it Truck Baseplate.

00:01:32.403 --> 00:01:38.475
Hanger: sketch on the Front plane. Use the notch edge as a reference.

00:01:39.025 --> 00:01:52.655
Two circles, 0.75 below the notch: Ø0.25 (axle) and Ø0.75 (hanger). Black = fully defined.

00:01:53.205 --> 00:01:59.579
Small circle: New, 8.5 in, Symmetric. That's the axle.

00:02:00.129 --> 00:02:06.073
Ring: Add to the axle part, 6 in, Symmetric. That's the hanger.

00:02:06.623 --> 00:02:10.373
Rename it Truck Hanger. Hide the deck to see better.

00:02:10.923 --> 00:02:20.583
Bushing: sketch on the baseplate's big bottom face. Dotted lines find the center.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:27.135
Two circles on the center: Ø1 and Ø0.375.

00:02:27.685 --> 00:02:33.223
Extrude both regions: New, 0.25 in, away from the baseplate.

00:02:33.773 --> 00:02:37.430
Rename it Bushing. It sits right under the baseplate.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:49.033
Kingpin: hide the bushing, show Sketch 6, extrude the small circle: Add to Truck Baseplate, 0.75 in.

00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:54.029
The kingpin runs through the bushing into the hanger.

00:02:54.579 --> 00:03:01.870
Fillet (Shift+F): baseplate edges, 0.125 in.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.543
Rounded edges look better and are safer to hold.

00:03:06.093 --> 00:03:10.668
Right-click the hanger → Edit appearance → light grey.

00:03:11.218 --> 00:03:20.227
Assign material: Aluminum - 356 for the baseplate and the hanger.

00:03:20.777 --> 00:03:26.512
Bushing: any color, material Polyurethane.

00:03:27.062 --> 00:03:37.221
Mass properties: select the 3 truck parts. Ours ≈ 0.55 lb.

00:03:37.771 --> 00:03:44.586
Board from below with one truck. You'll copy it in Lesson 2.4.
